{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/187188-physical-gates-to-the-shadowlands","id":187188,"title":"Physical Gates to the Shadowlands?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-03T09:48:03-07:00","id":187188,"title":"Physical Gates to the Shadowlands?","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> Running a Demon the Fallen game with a focus on the Shadowlands. I was wondering if, in any gameline, there was information on actual gateways that led to the Shadowlands, allowing someone to physically enter the realm of the dead without having to die and become a wraith. I know Slayers, Nagajara and the Giovanni (for example) can access the Shadowlands through their own powers and rituals, but what about actual doorways that have been said to exist in any line? I'd prefer reusing something already created than having to conduct a thorough review of literature of the real world mythology to identify those that might be suitable for the cWoD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T13:31:43-07:00","id":187367,"title":"","content":"sure why not, perhaps a mage left one open","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T15:15:21-07:00","id":187444,"title":"","content":"Given the sarcasm, let me further explain. :P<br /> <br /> The DtF Earthbound book gives an example of such a gateway on page 20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the African city of Axum, Azrael\u2019s single cult began swelling with members. Vast underground labyrinths and cities were built deep within the earth. Stone and dirt were ripped asunder, leaving behind massive channels scoring the landscape while huge black obelisks were erected upon the surface. Why? To commune with the dead. This cult, the Heitsi-Eibib, relied upon the \u201cwisdom\u201d of departed spirits to learn new knowledge, an idea championed by Azrael and his most favored servitors. These obelisks (many of which still exist today in Ethiopia) were used both as tools to speak to spirits and to open gateways to the shadowlands. </div> </div> </div>In the DtF Houses of the Fallen book, p.188:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [...Charon] authorized the construction of a number of direct gates from Haven to the living world. The gates did allow the numbers of souls entering Haven to grow significantly, but not spectacularly. Each gate was buried away in hidden caverns, deep in isolated forests and, in one notable case, undersea. This necessary security measure did slow the flow of souls, but it proved effective. In the end, Haven wasn\u2019t breached through one of the gates, but directly through the Veil. The gates endured the fall of Haven. Humanity\u2019s legends hint at their occasional rediscovery as well. Orpheus\u2019s descent into the underworld from Greek legends, Gilgamesh in Mesopotamian myths and the Thunder Twins of Hopi folklore all suggest that the gates remain active throughout the Slayers\u2019 imprisonment. Many returned Slayers are keen to find these gates again, because they have not yet managed to recall the lore necessary to enter Haven without assistance. Even the most recent of legends, however, suggest that the gates are buried far away from human eyes, in long forgotten caves, deep under ancient cities or possibly under the seas and deserts of the<br /> modern world. </div> </div> </div>So maybe other lines refer to similar things - I know Void Engineers closed various natural gateways to various umbral worlds (not tied to Demon's cosmology, obviously), so I figured there might be occurences related to the Shadowlands in other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T15:44:18-07:00","id":187460,"title":"","content":"IIRC, In the Giovanni Chronicle I think (or was it the Transylvania Chronicle) there was such a Gate. I don't recall in which Subterranean City -<b>Kaymakli</b> - the remaining Cappadocian were buried in, but some manage to escape Through the Shadowland to become the Harbinger of Skulls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T17:17:17-07:00","id":187524,"title":"","content":"The Giovanni vampires have a power, Ex-nihilo (a level 4 power), which open, temporarily, a door in the Shadowlands. Then, him and whoever he need, can physically enter in the Shadowlands.<br /> Your Fallen friends can make a pact with this guy (beware, you probably need to browbeat him a little before the accord) and then use its house as your personal &quot;portal&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T18:17:11-07:00","id":187558,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I\u2019d have to dig out my Wraith books to double-check, but here\u2019s what I recall (from an increasingly degenerative memory). <br /> <br /> I think what you\u2019re looking for is called a Shallowing. It\u2019s a place where the Shroud becomes so low that it ceases to exist. For example:<br /> <br /> Say a particularly spooky graveyard or haunted crossroads has a Shroud of \u2013 idk, say \u2013 2. While that\u2019s pretty low, maybe on certain times of the year it drops by two (like on Halloween), making the Shroud a whopping Zero. For a crafty (or demented) ST, this might be used as a McGuffin to get meatbags into the Shadowlands. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m getting the impression by \u201cgateway\u201d you mean some sort of fixed portal, like a necromantic version of the Stargate? Not really sure about that. I can make an educated guess in the context of Wraith, but I\u2019m only somewhat familiar with DtF. Earthbound are pretty BA though, so if anything could do it\u2026</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T22:12:24-07:00","id":187725,"title":"","content":"I do agree with Nazfool that a Shallowing is the most natural explanation in Wraith terms, I seem to recollect there still being a few possible place on earth where such Shallowings might exists, ie Shroud of 0 most of the time, though these would be exceedingly rare places of death. I don't think any line gives us any specific portals more allusions to them existing like the ones you quoted from DtF. The only direct one might be the mention of Kaymakli as said above.<br /> <br /> Of course then you have the Black Paths of Balor which are basically such gates and pathways that lead one to the Shadowlands, or even beyond it into Tempest, but these originate from the Dreaming. I also think there are similar paths to the Underworld that originate in the various Umbrae. But considering how DtF, unfortunately, almost completely ignores both Umbra and Dreaming these are not likely going to help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T04:58:23-07:00","id":187856,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I'm interested in fixed portals and not powers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> However, thanks a lot for the information on the Shallowing and the Black Paths of Balor - it might be very pertinent at some point in my game. There will be a need to let specific people around the globe accessing the Shadowlands for a specific purpose regarding the Black Labyrinth, and relying on personal powers to do so would be highly impractical. And Changelings and the various Umbrae (well, just a few of them) are considered in my game, so that's all good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:19:28-07:00","id":188021,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">@Possessed</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">In my mental decrepitude, it\u2019s good to know I can still recall random ghostly gaming minutia with some clarity. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> !</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">@BloodArmor</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">There\u2019s no reason why there can\u2019t be one these \u2018gateways\u2019 in your world. The troupe\u2019s search for one these mythical gateways would make a great story itself. By \u2018Black Labyrinth\u2019 do you mean the one from Werewolf (of BSD affiliation) or the one from Wraith (of Spectre affiliation)? No reason for this question, just curious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:44:33-07:00","id":188043,"title":"","content":"The one from Wraith, although I'm leveraging content from Werewolf as well and started from the Demon the Fallen origin of the Labyrinth with Charon (a Slayer is in search for him, and that led her to Stygia - although the fallen Charon and the Wraith Charon are two different entities). Grandma, the Children, BSDs and the Wyrm (which is the embodiment, in a sense, of GrandMa) are all tied to that Black Labyrinth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T10:19:25-07:00","id":188056,"title":"","content":"I once used the supposed spot where Enoch would have been built as a physical gate to the Shadowlands. Taking you to.. well Enoch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T11:34:45-07:00","id":188144,"title":"","content":"The Black Spiral Labyrinth from WtA is not the same as the Labyrinth in WtO. They're two very different things, one existing as a part of Malfeas in the Deep Umbra, the other is the layer of the Underworld just above Oblivion. While the Underworld is a part of the Umbra, it's a separate from the Deep Umbra. So unless you are radically changing the cosmology of the Umbra in your games, an ability that allows one to enter the Black Spiral Labyrinth wouldn't allow someone to enter the Underworld's Labyrinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T06:17:25-07:00","id":189337,"title":"","content":"According to the book of worlds, in order for a mage to travel to the low umbra, aka the Shadowlands, he needs to cast the agama sojourn effect (Entropy 4 life 2 spirit 3) which causes the caster <i>to temporarily die,</i> or hang on the edge between life and death. even then, they can't go any deeper without The aid of a wraith with argos.<br /> <br /> So bearing that in mind, a means to travel into the shadowlands made by mages is likely to be fraught with complications and very powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T07:13:23-07:00","id":189378,"title":"","content":"Oh well Aka, I knew I was in for changing quite a bit while attempting to merge so many game lines. :P<br /> <br /> Froggy, yeah, the players will need to take many things into consideration for that trip. They'll also need to rally some earthbounds who have enough long term sight to accept lending some &quot;help&quot; to stop GrandMaw's progression through Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:19:09-07:00","id":189596,"title":"","content":"Hello BloodArmor,<br /> <br /> If you don't mind using material from the New World of Darkness, you might look into the rules for Avernian Gates from Geist and or The Book of the Dead. Excellent stuff and very easy to convert to the OWOD. I use them all the time and haven't had a problem.<br /> <br /> Pax,<br /> <br /> Aeoris","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:39:58-07:00","id":190808,"title":"","content":"well, as a demon game you can always have gates to the underworld made, off the top of my head I want to say the supposed gate to eden in africa somewhere was supposed to lead to the underworld now, that may be wrong but I kinda remember reading it on rage across the heavens.<br /> <br /> demon the fallen gives you a bunch of stuff you can do, you can straight up imbue artifacts with demon powers and have fixed gates doted across the globe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T10:02:07-07:00","id":191493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_conta