anks, that's actually an awesome idea, given the fact it is based on our real world's lore!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T11:20:15-07:00","id":196983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/187188-physical-gates-to-the-shadowlands?p=189337#post189337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the book of worlds, in order for a mage to travel to the low umbra, aka the Shadowlands, he needs to cast the agama sojourn effect (Entropy 4 life 2 spirit 3) which causes the caster <i>to temporarily die,</i> or hang on the edge between life and death. even then, they can't go any deeper without The aid of a wraith with argos.<br /> <br /> So bearing that in mind, a means to travel into the shadowlands made by mages is likely to be fraught with complications and very powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Just jumping in for clarification...)<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that mages *can* travel deeper into the Low Umbra than just the Shadowlands: they'd either have to use Spirit:4 (and employ Cosmology w/a side order of &quot;Don't Get Lost&quot;) in the Sojourn (which they'd need to use when bringing others, anyway) or bump up to Spirit:5 and get there more directly... though the ambient dangers -- particularly if the Maelstrom and its associated warp-effects on True Magic(k) are in play -- are, of course, still as great, per your statement. Just adding for reference purposes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}